      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, as I mentioned above, I wasn\u0027t asking for a fully fledged specification but simply a more descriptive one-liner than \"entry 2 is a DTBO that is the VM DTBO\". For example, something along the lines of \"is a DTBO that pvmfw uses to validate physical devices that have been assigned to the guest\".\n\nAlso, this now states that:\n\n\u003e pvmfw will provision device tree with the VM DTBO\n\nwhich is simply wrong, isn\u0027t it?\n\nAnd I note that \"entry 2 *may* point\" (not \"*must*\") is inconsistent with your expectation of v1.1 mandating the presence of a VM DTBO, as you commented on go/gpar/660817.",
