      "side": 1,
      "message": "This error is raised when the header version doesn\u0027t support the entry index (which type-checking forces to always be _valid_, for at least one version) so I\u0027m worried that this error message might be misleading. Could we rework it to also contain the version (which, on a side note, it might be wise to turn into its own type, I recon?) e.g.\n```\nSelf::Unsupported((major, minor)) \u003d\u003e write!(f, \"Not supported by version {major}.{minor}\")\n```\nResulting in the combined error message:\n```\nInvalid Entry::VmDtbo entry: Not supported by version 1.0\n```\ninstead of what would currently be generated:\n```\nInvalid Entry::VmDtbo entry: Invalid entry index: 2\n```",
