      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T10:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you introduce a private method to get the `entries` as a slice, abstracting away the management of a maximum index, e.g.\n```\nfn entries(\u0026self) -\u003e Result\u003c\u0026[HeaderEntry]\u003e {\n    let last_entry \u003d match self.version {\n        Header::VERSION_1_0 \u003d\u003e Entry::DebugPolicy,\n        Header::VERSION_1_1 \u003d\u003e Entry::VmDtbo,\n        _ \u003d\u003e {\n            let (major, minor) \u003d self.version_tuple();\n            return Err(Error::UnsupportedVersion(major, minor));\n        }\n    };\n\n    Ok(\u0026self.entries[..\u003d(last_entry as usize)])\n}\n```\nwhich should then allow you to bound-check in the usual way\n```\nlet (offset, size) \u003d if let Some(e) \u003d self.entries().get(entry_index) {\n    (e.offset as usize, e.size as usize)\n} else {\n    return Err(Error::InvalidEntry(entry, ...));\n};\n```",
